  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Ju Kai Bei uses three Dragon-elephant Huge Strength Gu after he becomes a rank four Gu Master, and those three copies create three beast phantoms for him.",
        "chapters": [
          317
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_ju_kai_bei",
          "sys_gu_master"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "A dragon-elephant is a huge elephant with dragon’s blood, larger than a mammoth, and a mutated beast that lions and tigers avoid. Killing that ferocious beast gives a great chance of obtaining Dragon-elephant Huge Strength Gu. The Gu is rank four, above the rank three strength Gu Fang Yuan brings into the same match.",
        "chapters": [
          317
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "source-and-rank",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_strength_gu",
          "char_fang_yuan"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Ju Kai Bei must keep accumulating with Habitual Strength Gu, then summon the beast phantom, and even he does not know when it will appear. If he attacks and only one dragon-elephant strength appears, he has to accumulate again. Two dragon-elephant strength together is what lets him reclaim footing against Fang Yuan’s dual phantoms.",
        "chapters": [
          318
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "summoning-rhythm",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
